agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26056:The return contains 3 P1 and 2 P2 findings covering durability, validator correspondence, and inherited fork authority:
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26116:+    "git show 5e4ef522c91a478406931801eb8ddb7995758b22:matharc/v02/literature_base.py | rg -n 'getpid|register_at_fork|threading\\.local|held_paths|authorized_paths|allow_topic_transaction'",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26144:+      "detail": "An out-of-order cursor records a CURSOR_CONFLICT manual entry whose detail is derived from the then-current next_cursor. The runner still permits a later batch at the correct cursor to advance next_cursor and saves that state without validating the produced projection. On reload, the validator recomputes the historical conflict detail using the new next_cursor, or rejects when the manual cursor now equals next_cursor. The valid batch returns successfully even though the newly authenticated state is self-invalidating.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26145:+      "reproduction": "Start at c0. Call run with a batch from c1 to c2; it returns CURSOR_BLOCKED and records detail Expected cursor 'c0', received 'c1'. Then call run with a valid batch from c0 to c1; it returns successfully and persists next_cursor c1. The next next_cursor/manual_queue access or a new TopicObservationRunner raises 'cursor conflict manual entry names the current cursor'."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26151:+      "title": "A normal pending-to-observed upgrade authenticates historical evidence that the validator rejects",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26152:+      "detail": "A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26160:+      "detail": "Reentrancy and transaction authorization are stored in threading.local sets keyed only by path. They are not PID-bound and are not cleared with os.register_at_fork. A child forked by the thread holding the lock inherits held_paths and authorized_paths together with the flock file description. A normal child LiteratureBase import therefore takes the reentrant branch without acquiring independent exclusion; during a topic transaction it also passes the pending-journal check through inherited authorization. Parent and child can mutate the same manifests concurrently under shared flock ownership. This does not require arbitrary filesystem replacement or explicitly enabling authorization in the child.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26161:+      "reproduction": "On a POSIX host, enter literature_writer_lock(root, allow_topic_transaction=True), fork from that same thread, and have both parent and child perform distinct LiteratureBase(root).import_bytes calls while synchronizing them to overlap. The child sees root_key in its inherited held_paths, skips flock, retains inherited authorization, and can write concurrently with the parent."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26167:+  "failure_class": "transaction-durability-validator-correspondence-and-fork-inherited-lock-authority",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:26171:+    "No live power-loss, filesystem fault injection, or os.fork interleaving was executed.",
