149-## Reusable knowledge
150-
151-- A publication audit must search for actual `.tex`/`.pdf`, reconstruct every declared chunked artifact, compare declared size/SHA, and record unverifiable preflight claims separately. In the case audit, no manuscript existed; the ZIP and Base64 forms were truncated, so disposition was `scientific_closure: BLOCKED`, `evidence_integrity: INCOMPLETE`, `manuscript_state: NONE`, `technical_preflight: FAIL`, `human_signoff: PENDING`, `submission_route: UNDECIDED`. [Task 1]
152-- `cd src && bash reproduce_local_dynamics.sh` emitted archived values but did not cold-replay because `rebuild_local_dynamics_result.json` was missing. Generated numerical output is not proof-replay evidence when declared archive/expected records are missing. [Task 1]
153:- MathArc now rejects non-adjacent legacy claim pairs and duplicates; supports `\\matharcclaim{id}{revision}`; recursively collects `\\input`/`\\include` with cycle detection; blocks `.bib` without `.bbl`; and requires `INDEPENDENTLY_AUDITED` evidence plus nonempty human signoff before release-candidate readiness. Local publication tests passed 7/7, workflow policy and syntax compilation passed. [Task 2]
154:- `codex/publication-gates-hardening-20260831` was merged via PR #1; local and remote `main` matched `836dc6860f8f997e4e128bcd745c96b98c6b9b29`, and the remote feature branch was deleted. Untracked `agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/.ssot/` was preserved. [Task 2]
