codex
The current implementation confirms the main failure shapes: persisted lookup uses an `OR` and chooses by status; cursor-conflict detail recomputes from mutable `next_cursor`; recovery creates nested directories without parent fsync; retired-marker restoration is swallowed; `_save_state` writes before strict semantic reload; and the lock unconditionally unlocks on context exit. I’m now tracing the source/literature schemas and existing regression helpers so the repair remains compatible with the current `1.7` state contract and does not weaken legacy rejection.
